333,"urgency":0.5},{"title":"Health is wealth? Polymarket and Kalshi now host bets on measles and other US health crises","summary":"Experts warn of risks of platforms hosting bets tied to US public health – including vaccine mandates and drug trials The sign was pasted on a construction fence next to an elementary school in the Brooklyn borough of New York City. “Vaccines,” it proclaimed in bold capital letters against a blue star-spangled background – appearing, at first glance, to be like any other public health message on the importance of getting vaccinated. But at the bottom of the sign, in smaller letters, it read: “Will any state end vaccine markets?” It was accompanied by the logo for Polymarket, an online prediction market where users can log in to wager on the outcomes of nearly any event – including, now, public health. Continue reading...","link":"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/14/measles-kalshi-polymarket-betting","published":"Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:00:44 GMT","published_ts":1794657644.0,"source":"The Guardian World","category":"world","credibility":0.9,"sentiment":0.0,"direction":"neutral","confidence":0.98,"impact_score":22.8,"risk_level":"medium","coins":[],"event_risk":0.3333333333333333,"urgency":0.0},{"title":"‘Enough is enough’: rising number of deadly ebike battery fires spark fear in New York City","summary":"City has failed to build infrastructure that could reduce threat, and saw 400 fires, 83 injuries and 12 deaths this year Fires from lithium-ion batteries, which power ebikes and scooters, have become regular occurrences in New York, causing deaths and fear among residents, but the city has failed to build infrastructure that could reduce the threat. New York has seen a dramatic uptick this year in fires from the batteries. In 2025, there were 292 fires, 51 injuries and one death, according to the New York fire department (FDNY). This year, there have already been more than 400 fires, 83 injuries and 12 deaths. Continue reading...","link":"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/14/new-york-city-ebike-battery-fires-deaths","published":"Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:00:44 GMT","published_ts":1794657644.0,"source":"The Guardian World","category":"world","credibility":0.9,"sentiment":0.0,"direction":"neutral","confidence":0.615,"impact_score":10.8,"risk_level":"low","coins":[],"event_risk":0.0,"urgency":0.0},{"title":"XRP ETF Outflows Hit an 8-Month High. December Rarely Brings Relief","summary":"US spot XRP ETFs lost $19.13 million in the week ending November 13. It was their largest weekly outflow in 8 months, and it came as the altcoin fell below $1.00. The funds have now posted 2 straight weeks of outflows. XRP has also lost 20% so far in November, CryptoRank data shows. Past Decembers The post XRP ETF Outflows Hit an 8-Month High. December Rarely Brings Relief appeared first on BeInCrypto .","link":"https://beincrypto.com/xrp-etf-outflows-8-month-high/","published":"Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000","published_ts":1794657600.0,"source":"BeInCrypto","category":"crypto","credibility":0.8,"sentiment":-1.0,"direction":"negative","confidence":0.82,"impact_score":57.6,"risk_level":"low","coins":["XRP"],"event_risk":0.0,"urgency":0.0},{"title":"China’s hottest stocks these days have one thing in common: names that sound like sheep","summary":"Shares of fish processors, lighting manufacturers and appliance makers have soared ahead of the Year of the Sheep. Investor appetite has had little to do with the status of their businesses.","link":"https://www.marketwatch.com/story/chinas-hottest-stocks-these-days-have-one-thing-in-common-names-that-sound-like-sheep-6176e521?mod=mw_rss_topstories","published":"Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:00:00 GMT","published_ts":1794657600.0,"source":"MarketWatch","category":"macro","credibility":0.9,"sentiment":1.0,"direction":"positive","confidence":0.735,"impact_score":58.8,"risk_level":"low","coins":[],"event_risk":0.0,"urgency":0.0},{"title":"9 Reasons Bitcoin Crashed From $81K to